# The evidence pack (.claude/bin/evidence, /verify-feature).
# Duplicated code (jscpd 5, see the adapters). $KIT_BASE is the base branch. KIT_DUPLICATES fails on clones the
# branch adds against the base; legacy clones never block. KIT_DUPLICATES_RELATED does the same for the uncommitted
# files only (the edit hook). KIT_SIMILAR lists similar functions; it never fails.
KIT_DUPLICATES=""
KIT_DUPLICATES_RELATED=""
KIT_SIMILAR=""

# Files whose change makes a later review or verify round cover the whole branch again (.claude/bin/evidence scope):
# auth, migrations, public routes. Shell patterns, separated by spaces.
KIT_CONTRACT_PATTERNS=""

# /verify-feature (all optional; a missing one is recorded as "not configured" in the evidence pack).
# KIT_SEED resets and seeds a local database and prints "seed: <version>". KIT_E2E runs the e2e suite against it.
# KIT_TEST_MOCKED runs the suite with external dependencies replaced and prints "mocked: <what>".
# KIT_SCREENSHOTS writes <AC-ID>-<step>-<desktop|mobile>$KIT_SCREENSHOT_SUFFIX.png into $KIT_SCREENSHOT_DIR.
# KIT_SETUP prepares a fresh worktree of the base branch (the install) for the base-branch screenshots.
# KIT_APP_URL is where the app runs locally, for scripts that need it.
KIT_SEED=""
KIT_E2E=""
KIT_TEST_MOCKED=""
KIT_SCREENSHOTS=""
# Only the e2e tests a change affects (pull requests; the whole suite runs after merge with `evidence data --all`).
# KIT_E2E_RELATED and KIT_SCREENSHOTS_RELATED get the selected test files appended. KIT_E2E_PATTERNS says which files
# are e2e tests. A test runs when its file changed, or when it names a feature (SHOP in SHOP-AC1) whose criterion IDs
# the diff adds. A change to a file in KIT_E2E_FULL_PATTERNS (shared setup), or to code no e2e test maps to, runs
# everything; a change to only tests and docs runs no e2e. Without KIT_E2E_RELATED the whole suite always runs.
# KIT_E2E_MAP names a file outside .claude/ (for example .kit/e2e-map.tsv) that maps source paths to the e2e tests
# that cover them, one row per area: "<source pattern> TAB <e2e test patterns, all, or ->". The first matching row
# wins; "-" means no e2e test covers it. With a map, a changed source file without a row runs everything, and the
# verify gate e2e-map fails while a row matches no file. See docs/customizing.md, "Select e2e tests with a map".
KIT_E2E_MAP=""
# The stack stage (docs/customizing.md, "The stack stage"): the seed, the e2e tests with their screenshots, and the
# mutation tests run once per stack, on its top layer, as the last check before the merge: "ci" (the default;
# .github/workflows/stack-checks.yml, which must be on the default branch), "local" (in this checkout), or "off"
# (verify runs the seed and the e2e tests itself, as before, and there are no mutation tests).
KIT_STACK_CHECKS="ci"
# Mutation tests on the changed lines: KIT_MUTATION gets the changed ranges appended as one comma-separated argument
# ("src/a.ts:10-14,src/b.ts:3-3"); KIT_MUTATION_FILES prints its report as "<file> TAB <line> TAB <mutator> TAB
# <status>" (Killed, Timeout, Survived, NoCoverage). The score is killed and timed-out mutants over all on the changed
# lines; below KIT_MUTATION_THRESHOLD the stage is red. Equivalent mutants a person accepts go into
# KIT_MUTATION_EXCEPTIONS ("<file> TAB <line> TAB <mutator> TAB <reason>"), a committed file outside .claude/.
KIT_MUTATION=""
KIT_MUTATION_FILES=""
KIT_MUTATION_THRESHOLD="60"
KIT_MUTATION_EXCEPTIONS=".kit/mutation-exceptions.tsv"
KIT_E2E_RELATED=""
KIT_SCREENSHOTS_RELATED=""
KIT_E2E_PATTERNS=""
# JUnit report that KIT_E2E writes, relative to the package; `evidence data` adds its results to the matrix's tests.
KIT_E2E_REPORT=""
KIT_E2E_FULL_PATTERNS=""
KIT_SETUP=""
# An env file (path from the root) whose variables the base-branch screenshot run gets, for example the test stack's
# database and Redis URLs. It is read for that run only and never copied into the worktree. When no e2e test on
# the base names the change's feature, the base run is skipped and recorded as "n/a: base has no <FEATURE>".
KIT_BASE_ENV=""
KIT_APP_URL=""
# The test stack's own resources, exported to KIT_SEED, KIT_E2E and KIT_SCREENSHOTS: a database name, a Redis db
# number and a port. Commands that reset state reset only these (flush this Redis db, not the server). See
# docs/customizing.md, "Isolate the test stack".
KIT_RUN_DB=""
KIT_RUN_REDIS_DB=""
KIT_RUN_PORT=""

# Failed verify rounds per class before /verify-feature asks (.claude/bin/gate round). kit false positives never
# count, spec changes always ask, and at autonomous test and hotfix rounds continue past the limit.
KIT_VERIFY_ROUNDS="test:3 hotfix:2"
